A||N||7||kornholio||powering 12v fog lights from fusebox?||||5
Z||000000||kornholio||11-26-1999||02:15 PM||||I just got my fog lights today and I was wondering if it is possible to splice the 12v power wire to a wire in the fusebox instead of running a wire the length of the vehicle to the positive battery terminal.  Each light draws about 4.3 amps, so a total of 8.6 amps.  There is a fuse on the power wire (15 amps).  If it is possible, which wire should I splice into---&gt;how many amps (5,10,20,25)?  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||RZURCTN||11-26-1999||03:01 PM||||I would use a 20 or 25 amp fuse if possible, your foglight circuit already has a fuse so that will keep them good.  Find a fuse that is hot only when the key is in the "on" position.  You won't want to forget that your foglights are on someday and drain your battery.  Especailly if you have a separate switch from that of your headlights.  There should be a fuse for your headlights, I'd just use that one!  Good luck and good fun!!<P>P.S.:  Let us know how they work and look!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||11-26-1999||03:35 PM||||I forgot to ask...Is it safe to power fog lights from the fuse box??  These lights are 55w (I don't know if that's important or not).  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||11-26-1999||05:06 PM||||Mine are hooked up to the fuse box, with a in-line fuse, and a lighted switch. It works good.<P>Get the lighted switch!||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||11-26-1999||05:06 PM||||Mine are hooked up to the fuse box, with a in-line fuse, and a lighted switch. It works good.<P>Get the lighted switch!||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||11-26-1999||05:10 PM||||DXR_DAD,<BR>Mine came with a blue lighted switch...it looks cool.  Which fuse did you hook your fog lights up to?||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||11-26-1999||09:39 PM||||I don't like the idea of running another 8-10 amps inside the car.  Feel the wire after the lights have been on for a while, and you may see what I mean.  As for splicing into the headlights or tapping off the ignition switch, Ford just issued a recall for the headlight switches in 89-95 foglight equipped cars (only 35 watt foglights).  They used the headlight switch for the fogs also.  Seems the headlight switch was burning up.  I used a relay with the relay getting power from the cigarette lighter light (only comes on when the parking/headlights are on).  I then used a 12 gauge wire from the top of my battery, with an in-line fuse.  I have a dual connection batery, so it's easy.  I ran the 12 gauge wire along the right hand coolant pipe inside some corrugated plasic tubing.  I mounted the rocker switch under the trunk switch.  I'm no electrical engineer, but we don't need any more burnt up fieros, either.  <p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 11-26-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||11-26-1999||11:13 PM||||Next to the radio fuse there are two plugs, they both say: (bat) I have had these lights hooked up for 2yr and had no problems. My switch is orangeish? in color, matched the fiero dash lights good.||||reg||1
